From fe9663234e5114ef5a98c1aa718f238a806dfec8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 15:52:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: qcom-spmi-adc-tm5: stop requiring IIO_VAL_INT from a
 processed read

Every get_temp on an adc-tm zone fails with -EINVAL, and the thermal core says
so once per zone at boot:

	thermal thermal_zone19: Temperature check failed (-22)

while the same channel read straight from IIO gives a sane value:

	/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:device0/in_temp_skin_therm_input -> 36666

adc_tm5_get_temp() checks that iio_read_channel_processed() returned
IIO_VAL_INT. That was true until commit 05f958d003c9 ("iio: Improve
iio_read_channel_processed_scale() precision"), which replaced

	*val *= scale;
	return ret;

with a call to the new iio_multiply_value() helper, and that returns 0 on
success rather than passing the driver's value type back up. IIO_VAL_INT is 1,
so the check now rejects every successful read. The RAW fallback branch of the
same function returns 0 as well, so there is no value type left to check
against; the return is 0-or-negative-errno now and the value is in *temp
either way.

No other caller of iio_read_channel_processed() in the tree tests the return
for a value type.

Fixes: 05f958d003c9 ("iio: Improve iio_read_channel_processed_scale() precision")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/thermal/qcom/qcom-spmi-adc-tm5.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thermal/qcom/qcom-spmi-adc-tm5.c b/drivers/thermal/qcom/qcom-spmi-adc-tm5.c
index d7f2e6ca92c2..d1b086737bcd 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/qcom/qcom-spmi-adc-tm5.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/qcom/qcom-spmi-adc-tm5.c
@@ -369,9 +369,6 @@ static int adc_tm5_get_temp(struct thermal_zone_device *tz, int *temp)
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
-	if (ret != IIO_VAL_INT)
-		return -EINVAL;
-
 	return 0;
 }
 
-- 
2.55.0

